---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title={'Career milestones — Felipe Alves'}
  description={'Selected career milestones from Felipe Alves across data, product and transformation.'}
  ogDescription={'A selective career timeline across data, product and transformation.'}
  ogType="website"
  css={['styles', 'responsive', 'enhancements', 'site-fixes']}
  bodyClass="milestones-page"
  script="script"
  current="milestones"
>
<main>
    <section class="milestones-hero section-shell">
      <div class="reveal"><span class="eyebrow">Selected career milestones</span><h1>From the <span>data layer</span> upward.</h1><p>A deliberately selective timeline: the moments that changed the kind of problems I could solve, rather than every job title or project I touched.</p></div>
      <aside class="milestone-aside reveal delay-1"><strong>Filter the story.</strong>Data, product and transformation have overlapped throughout my career, but not equally at every stage. The filters below show the progression without turning this into another CV.</aside>
    </section>

    <section class="milestone-controls-wrap"><div class="section-shell milestone-controls" role="tablist" aria-label="Filter career milestones"><button class="milestone-filter active" data-milestone-lens="all" role="tab" aria-selected="true">All</button><button class="milestone-filter" data-milestone-lens="data" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Data & analytics</button><button class="milestone-filter" data-milestone-lens="product" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Product</button><button class="milestone-filter" data-milestone-lens="transformation" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Transformation</button><span class="milestone-count" id="milestone-count" aria-live="polite">9 selected milestones</span></div></section>

    <section class="milestone-list section-shell" id="milestones">
      <article class="milestone-item reveal" data-milestone-tags="data"><div class="milestone-year">2016</div><div class="milestone-content"><div class="milestone-tags"><span class="milestone-tag">Data</span></div><h2>Started where business logic becomes data.</h2><p>Built my foundation at CCEE in Oracle, SQL/PLSQL, ETL and production systems supporting a highly regulated electricity market. It was less glamorous than product strategy—and probably more useful: learning how calculation logic, data models and operational systems actually behave under real constraints.</p><div class="milestone-proof"><span>Oracle</span><span>·</span><span>SQL/PLSQL</span><span>·</span><span>ETL</span><span>·</span><span>OLTP / ODS / DW</span></div></div></article>

      <article class="milestone-item reveal" data-milestone-tags="data transformation"><div class="milestone-year">2017–19</div><div class="milestone-content"><div class="milestone-tags"><span class="milestone-tag">Data</span><span class="milestone-tag">Transformation</span></div><h2>Moved from writing queries to designing systems.</h2><p>Expanded from data development into systems analysis: requirements, UML/BPMN/DFD, testing strategy, transactional and reporting models, and production troubleshooting. The recurring pattern was already emerging—translate business rules into something technical teams can implement and validate.</p><div class="milestone-proof"><span>Systems analysis</span><span>·</span><span>data modelling</span><span>·</span><span>testing</span></div></div></article>

      <article class="milestone-item reveal" data-milestone-tags="data transformation"><div class="milestone-year">2019</div><div class="milestone-content"><div class="milestone-tags"><span class="milestone-tag">Data</span><span class="milestone-tag">Transformation</span></div><h2>Shifted from systems to market rules.</h2><p>As an Energy Market Analyst, the work moved upstream: legislative and regulatory changes had to become calculation algebra, pricing and settlement logic, KPIs and impact analysis.</p><div class="milestone-proof"><span>regulation → algebra</span><span>·</span><span>pricing & settlement</span><span>·</span><span>leadership reporting</span></div><a class="milestone-source" href="https://www.ccee.org.br/mercado/regras-de-comercializacao" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Public context · CCEE trading rules ↗</a></div></article>

      <article class="milestone-item reveal" data-milestone-tags="data transformation"><div class="milestone-year">2020</div><div class="milestone-content"><div class="milestone-tags"><span class="milestone-tag">Data</span><span class="milestone-tag">Transformation</span></div><h2>Started working on risk before it became a dashboard.</h2><p>Moved into a Business Analyst role bridging Internal Audit, Market Security and technical teams. The work combined risk questions with data definitions, SQL, ETL, analytical design and executive communication.</p><div class="milestone-proof"><span>risk & compliance</span><span>·</span><span>advanced SQL</span><span>·</span><span>analytics PoCs</span></div></div></article>

      <article class="milestone-item reveal" data-milestone-tags="data transformation"><div class="milestone-year">2021–22</div><div class="milestone-content"><div class="milestone-tags"><span class="milestone-tag">Data</span><span class="milestone-tag">Transformation</span></div><h2>Helped shape an integrated market-risk framework while it was still being formed.</h2><p>Led end-to-end delivery work on CCEE's Integrated Risk Analysis, contributing across requirements, data modelling, ETL and SAS analytics. Public CCEE material later documented the framework at 60+ metrics, 10 indicators and three pillars.</p><div class="milestone-proof"><span>Integrated Risk Analysis</span><span>·</span><span>SAS</span><span>·</span><span>−32% internal compliance-risk measure</span></div><a class="milestone-source" href="https://www.ccee.org.br/documents/80415/919440/20230316_Apresenta%C3%A7%C3%A3o_EncontroCCEE_Madalena.pdf/635a16e3-7eb6-cb47-7f46-f53fc122ef56" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Public continuation · CCEE ARI presentation ↗</a></div></article>

      <article class="milestone-item reveal" data-milestone-tags="product transformation"><div class="milestone-year">2022</div><div class="milestone-content"><div class="milestone-tags"><span class="milestone-tag">Product</span><span class="milestone-tag">Transformation</span></div><h2>Changed industries, countries and level of abstraction at once.</h2><p>Moved from Brazil's electricity market to Dubai aviation and into Technical Product Ownership at Emirates / dnata. The technical foundation stayed useful, but the job became orchestration across operational users, engineering, delivery, vendors and enterprise priorities.</p><div class="milestone-proof"><span>Dubai</span><span>·</span><span>enterprise aviation</span><span>·</span><span>2 Scrum teams</span></div></div></article>

      <article class="milestone-item reveal" data-milestone-tags="product transformation"><div class="milestone-year">2024–25</div><div class="milestone-content"><div class="milestone-tags"><span class="milestone-tag">Product</span><span class="milestone-tag">Transformation</span></div><h2>Turned a legacy-system rewrite into product choices.</h2><p>Led extended discovery for the Baggage Reconciliation System modernisation, producing 75 features, defining the MVP and a five-year roadmap, and supporting RFI/RFP work.</p><div class="milestone-proof"><span>75 features</span><span>·</span><span>MVP scoped</span><span>·</span><span>5-year roadmap</span></div><a class="milestone-source" href="https://www.dnata.com/media-centre/dnata-handles-over-82-million-bags-through-dubai-international-airport-dxb-in-2022/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Operating scale · dnata 82M+ bags at DXB ↗</a></div></article>

      <article class="milestone-item reveal" data-milestone-tags="product"><div class="milestone-year">2025</div><div class="milestone-content"><div class="milestone-tags"><span class="milestone-tag">Product</span></div><h2>Expanded leadership without pretending it was line management.</h2><p>Alongside product ownership, I mentored junior Product Owners and team members, ran knowledge-transfer sessions, led delivery ceremonies and acted as a frequent point of contact across engineering and QA.</p><div class="milestone-proof"><span>mentoring</span><span>·</span><span>PI planning</span><span>·</span><span>backlog & delivery leadership</span></div></div></article>

      <article class="milestone-item reveal" data-milestone-tags="data product transformation"><div class="milestone-year">2026 — now</div><div class="milestone-content"><div class="milestone-tags"><span class="milestone-tag">Data</span><span class="milestone-tag">Product</span><span class="milestone-tag">Transformation</span></div><h2>Finance Data Analytics Specialist · Emirates</h2><p>Moved into Group Finance data products: co-owning Cash Flow Forecasting with Data Science, investigating production business logic, and supporting a 40+ application eInvoicing transformation through programme reporting, data integration and status/KPI standardisation.</p><div class="milestone-proof"><span>Group Finance</span><span>·</span><span>Dataiku</span><span>·</span><span>Treasury</span><span>·</span><span>40+ applications</span><span>·</span><span>QMetry / Jira</span></div><a class="milestone-source" href="https://mof.gov.ae/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/UAE-Electronic-Invoicing-Guidelines_V-1.1-01June2026.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">National eInvoicing context · UAE Ministry of Finance ↗</a></div></article>
    </section>

    <section class="milestone-coda section-shell reveal"><span class="eyebrow">The through-line</span><h2>The titles changed. The useful role stayed surprisingly consistent.</h2><p>Understand the business rule, get close enough to the data and systems to challenge it, then make the problem clear enough for people with different incentives and expertise to move together.</p></section>
  </main>
</Base>
